# Files that end up inside a container must keep LF endings.
#
# On a Windows checkout git hands out CRLF, and a shell that reads "set -e\r"
# answers "Illegal option -": the API container exited before it ever reached a
# migration. The container runs Linux whatever the developer's machine runs, so
# these endings are not a preference.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Keep the PDF out of the line-ending machinery entirely.
*.pdf binary
